  "question": {
    "text": "If in case of a radio isotope the value of half-life \\(\\left(T_{1/2}\\right)\\) and decay constant \\((\\lambda)\\) are identical in magnitude, then their value should be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kmyFG",
      "text": "\\(0.693 / 2\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Jl1x8",
      "text": "\\((0.693)^{1 / 2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xPj0X",
      "text": "\\((0.693)^2\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uVcce",
      "text": "0.693",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: For a radio decay \\(T_{1 / 2}=\\frac{0.693}{\\lambda}\\)\nIf \\(T_{1 / 2}=\\lambda=x\\) then \\(\\mathrm{x}=\\frac{0.693}{\\mathrm{x}}\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}^2=0.693, \\quad \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{T}_{1 / 2}=\\lambda=(0.693)^{1 / 2}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
